b49-563f-ad11-de767d89d89b" :question/math-academy-id "q-288817" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+24x+15=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the product of its solutions." :question/worked-solution "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=5,\\,b=24,\\,c=15.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{a} & =\\frac{15}{5}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288817/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c16a30bc-0c1a-54f2-95d6-47edb0c85736"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288817"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288819/selection/c90f90a417565b483a3cef7341fc5664b4f6e019e1db04f561426df0a30a5718" :answer/id #uuid "e612dcc1-a5a7-5eb7-97a8-cd782c2c87ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\,395" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288819/selection/d0ee7905065fbf2847f5402a115c76bad796504d33e2080a2cc4b24ed03e1225" :answer/id #uuid "52718b2c-82f8-5ba5-9b8a-5d80011ed86c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-8\\,395}{146}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288819/selection/7c28f62627d2c84aa9ac93afaef5863c6445e792ea8ee736a7b0ef90c5e2e4d2" :answer/id #uuid "390abde6-1d1e-547d-b8bf-eb4b212eba66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{146}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288819/selection/22a4cac8ed7be20e7e337d7aca994e17f28d52d64f1ace939b6517045a8d8c23" :answer/id #uuid "c70e1173-a89f-5d18-9a13-ca9b6dfa78c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,395" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288819/selection/6c91da3382340c13acd6bb94ebc1dcb21ba4e5283cec450e58aeab685a901bfc" :answer/id #uuid "20046d4e-5836-5fae-b719-fd9691d34151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2)\\cdot 8\\,395" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288819/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11eda378-9d35-5206-8052-158756b70caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-288819/selection/c90f90a417565b483a3cef7341fc5664b4f6e019e1db04f561426df0a30a5718" :answer-field/choices ["q-288819/selection/c90f90a417565b483a3cef7341fc5664b4f6e019e1db04f561426df0a30a5718" "q-288819/selection/d0ee7905065fbf2847f5402a115c76bad796504d33e2080a2cc4b24ed03e1225" "q-288819/selection/7c28f62627d2c84aa9ac93afaef5863c6445e792ea8ee736a7b0ef90c5e2e4d2" "q-288819/selection/22a4cac8ed7be20e7e337d7aca994e17f28d52d64f1ace939b6517045a8d8c23" "q-288819/selection/6c91da3382340c13acd6bb94ebc1dcb21ba4e5283cec450e58aeab685a901bfc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288819" :question/id #uuid "a60a042a-0631-504b-9c2c-28fdb04eadac" :question/math-academy-id "q-288819" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+146x-8\\,395=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the product of its solutions." :question/worked-solution "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=1,\\,b=146,\\,c=-8\\,395.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{a} & =\\frac{(-8\\,395)}{1}=-8\\,395.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288819/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c16a30bc-0c1a-54f2-95d6-47edb0c85736"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288819"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288829/field-1/8184c605927351a6f5235bd53186d63412f04e4fe1488ca9d1e9aaf77dfe863b" :answer/id #uuid "f42f8152-f037-57bd-9198-0033616e91d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x^2-40x-60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288829/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "63a66eea-a4ee-51f5-aef8-71917a950acb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288829/field-1/8184c605927351a6f5235bd53186d63412f04e4fe1488ca9d1e9aaf77dfe863b" :answer-field/choices ["q-288829/field-1/8184c605927351a6f5235bd53186d63412f04e4fe1488ca9d1e9aaf77dfe863b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288829" :question/id #uuid "f19f761f-113c-5a3e-a541-96b268d77a65" :question/math-academy-id "q-288829" :question/problem "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $5.$ The sum of the solutions equals $8,$ and the product of the solutions equals $-12.$ Find the equation.\n\nThe equation is\n{{field-1}}  \n$=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's use the given information to determine the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ in this case:\n\n- We're told that the quadratic coefficient equals $5.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\na=5.\n$$\n\n- We're told that the sum of the roots equals $8.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =-\\frac{b}{a} \\\\ 8 & =-\\frac{b}{5} \\\\ -40 & =b \\\\ b & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- We're told that the product of the roots equals $-12.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12 & =\\frac{c}{a} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{c}{5} \\\\ -60 & =c \\\\ c & =-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation has coefficients\n\n$$\na=5,\\,b=-40,\\,c=-60\n$$\n\nand the equation is\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}-40x-60=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288829/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18c41022-916d-5d5c-89e6-ebfdc56f8fe3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288829"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288830/field-1/b99fc02468767cf07a3e6586eb7d00c1c776951061cb7a74b8af332dbb80fa2f" :answer/id #uuid "68a391b3-9624-5674-b6f2-0f092c94c644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x^2+30x-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288830/field-1/fec8c1ed82536f48c06276587e3878f6e620e73fcfb96ebf85d4c0ddd01b8b78" :answer/id #uuid "7d644c43-4a47-5527-91ba-c5b4d8dd2539" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x^2-30x-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288830/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "63fa0792-d53e-54a2-bc52-75f6888dd2ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288830/field-1/b99fc02468767cf07a3e6586eb7d00c1c776951061cb7a74b8af332dbb80fa2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-288830/field-1/b99fc02468767cf07a3e6586eb7d00c1c776951061cb7a74b8af332dbb80fa2f" "q-288830/field-1/fec8c1ed82536f48c06276587e3878f6e620e73fcfb96ebf85d4c0ddd01b8b78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288830" :question/id #uuid "383bb39e-8419-59c8-b054-4e4ff33cd3cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-288830" :question/problem "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $6.$ The sum of the solutions equals $-5,$ and the product of the solutions equals $-7.$ Find the equation.\n\nThe equation is\n{{field-1}}  \n$=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's use the given information to determine the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ in this case:\n\n- We're told that the quadratic coefficient equals $6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\na=6.\n$$\n\n- We're told that the sum of the roots equals $-5.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & =-\\frac{b}{a} \\\\ -5 & =-\\frac{b}{6} \\\\ 30 & =b \\\\ b & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- We're told that the product of the roots equals $-7.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7 & =\\frac{c}{a} \\\\ -7 & =\\frac{c}{6} \\\\ -42 & =c \\\\ c & =-42.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation has coefficients\n\n$$\na=6,\\,b=30,\\,c=-42\n$$\n\nand the equation is\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+30x-42=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288830/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18c41022-916d-5d5c-89e6-ebfdc56f8fe3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288830"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288851/field-1/74a06c74058a3bc88684af86bfa636048e65ccdf6cf6e10f72a7ba6d343ba52f" :answer/id #uuid "87e54de7-a16b-521a-bac4-29849153cca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^2+8x+20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288851/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6b59641-f342-5a49-a30a-58aecb8dc116" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288851/field-1/74a06c74058a3bc88684af86bfa636048e65ccdf6cf6e10f72a7ba6d343ba52f" :answer-field/choices ["q-288851/field-1/74a06c74058a3bc88684af86bfa636048e65ccdf6cf6e10f72a7ba6d343ba52f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288851" :question/id #uuid "788ba504-16c1-5c01-835a-cdf05791424c" :question/math-academy-id "q-288851" :question/problem "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $1.$ The sum of the solutions equals $-8,$ and the product of the solutions equals $20.$ Find the equation.\n\nThe equation is\n{{field-1}}\n$=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's use the given information to determine the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ in this case:\n\n- We're told that the quadratic coefficient equals $1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\na=1.\n$$\n\n- We're told that the sum of the roots equals $-8.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =-\\frac{b}{a} \\\\ -8 & =-\\frac{b}{1} \\\\ 8 & =b \\\\ b & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- We're told that the product of the roots equals $20.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20 & =\\frac{c}{a} \\\\ 20 & =\\frac{c}{1} \\\\ c & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation has coefficients\n\n$$\na=1,\\,b=8,\\,c=20\n$$\n\nand the equation is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+8x+20=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288851/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18c41022-916d-5d5c-89e6-ebfdc56f8fe3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288851"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
